hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16696","He said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, al-Thawri narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Abu Ayyash al-Zuraqi, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Usfan. The polytheists faced us, over them Khalid ibn al-Walid, and they were between us and the qiblah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in Zuhr. They said: They were in a state; had we seized their unawares. Then they said: There comes upon them now a prayer dearer to them than their sons and themselves. He said: Jibril, peace be upon him, descended with these verses between Zuhr and Asr: And when you are among them and establish for them the prayer. He said: It came, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered them and they took weapons. He said: We lined behind him two rows. He said: Then he bowed, and we bowed all together. Then he raised, and we raised all together. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated with the row next to him, while the others stood guarding them. When they prostrated and stood, the others sat and prostrated in their place. Then these advanced to the positions of these, and these came to the positions of these. He said: Then he bowed, and they bowed all together. Then he raised, and they raised all together. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated, and the row next to him, while the others stood guarding them. When he sat, the others sat and prostrated. He greeted them, then finished. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed it twice, once at Usfan and once in the land of Banu Sulaym."
"16697","He said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Mansur, he said: I heard Mujahid narrating from Abu Ayyash al-Zuraqi, he said: Shubah said: He wrote it to me, I read it to him, and heard it from him narrating it, but I memorized it from the book that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in battle lines against the enemy at Usfan, and over the polytheists was Khalid ibn al-Walid. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led them in Zuhr. Then the polytheists said: They have a prayer after this dearer to them than their sons and wealth. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led them in Asr and lined them two rows behind him. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bowed with them all together. When they raised their heads, the row next to him prostrated, and the others stood. When they raised their heads, the rear row prostrated for their bowing with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Then the front row moved back, and the rear row moved forward, and each stood in the place of his fellow. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bowed with them all together. When they raised their heads from bowing, the row next to him prostrated, and the others stood. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) greeted them."
"16698","He said: Muammal narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Abu Ayyash al-Zuraqi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the fear prayer while the polytheists were between them and the qiblah, twice, once in the land of Banu Sulaym and once at Usfan."
"16699","He said: Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Ayyash, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says in the morning: There is no god but Allah alone, no partner for Him; His is dominion and His is praise, and He is over all things powerful, shall have as the freeing of a slave from the children of Ismail, ten good deeds written for him thereby, ten evil deeds removed from him thereby, ten degrees raised for him thereby, and shall be in protection from Satan until evening. When evening comes, the like of that until morning. He said: A man saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in what the sleeper sees and said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Ayyash narrates from you such-and-such. He said: Abu Ayyash spoke the truth."
